  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is probably covered elsewhere. I've found that opening the UI menu window to browse Worlds or Avatars, has an annoying bug where using the left controller trigger to scroll down a menu page, works as intended but only so far. If the content is at the bottom of a page, the moment I try to launch a world or click a menu item, the page I'm looking at just auto scrolls back to its start position. This is very frustrating. The only method I've found to deal with this, is to use the small icons button, which condenses a page into a solid non-scrollable grid, which works as intended. Speaking with a friend who uses a Vive, it was suggested that my issue may well be Quest 2 specific.",
